.TH ONEC-FETCH 1 "October 2026" "onec-fetch 2.0.0"
.SH NAME
onec-fetch \- system information in 1C / OneScript
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B onec-fetch
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Displays an OS logo and system information using a module engine written in
1C / OneScript. The bundled runtime is installed under /opt/onec-fetch.
Optional system utilities expose additional hardware and desktop information.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --all --debug
Select all 76 modules and show reasons for unavailable data.
.TP
.BI "-s " CPU:GPU:Memory
Select modules and their order.
.TP
.BI "-c " config.jsonc
Read a JSON or JSONC configuration.
.TP
.B --json
Print data, sources and status using schema version 2.
.TP
.B --json=legacy
Print the earlier flat JSON keys.
.TP
.B --list-modules
List the available module identifiers.
.TP
.B --list-logos
List built-in logos.
.TP
.BI --logo= NAME
Select a logo, including auto or 1c.
.TP
.B --no-color --no-logo
Disable colors or the logo.
.TP
.B --allow-network
Explicitly enable PublicIp and Weather HTTP requests.
.TP
.BI --command= COMMAND
Provide a shell command. It runs only when Command is selected.
.TP
.B --timeout=3000 --interval=200
Per-command timeout and shared Linux sampling interval, in milliseconds.
.TP
.B --help
Print usage and additional options.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B /opt/onec-fetch/config/example.jsonc
Example configuration. No automatic configuration is loaded.
.TP
.B /opt/onec-fetch/docs/
Module limits and JSON documentation.
.TP
.B /opt/onec-fetch/licenses/
Bundled runtime licenses and source links.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.B NO_COLOR
Disables ANSI color unless --color is explicitly given.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on a completed report, including unavailable module data; 2 on invalid
arguments, invalid configuration or a fatal program error.
.SH SEE ALSO
https://github.com/SPAWNRYS-ban/onec-fetch
